A("# Test report v2 — Laya family-law decision graph, layman-proof two-stage build")
A("")
A("**Date:** 2026-11-26. **v2 file:** `laya-crpc-bns-section-decision-tree-v2.json` (valid JSON, `python json.load` passes; v1 untouched).")
A("")
A("## The two-stage design (as the user specified it)")
A("")
A("**STAGE 1 — Layman to article/section:** first pick ALL layman words/phrases and fetch them into article-section format. Convert every layman expression into legal terms, then map legal terms to section(s) via Laya choice questions. The user asks in layman format — \"my husband is not giving me money\", \"he took my gold and cash and won't return it\", \"they are throwing me out of the house\", \"who will get my daughter\", \"I need money for my child\", \"he beats me / threatens me\".")
A("")
A("**STAGE 2 — Recheck inside the article section:** after Stage 1 picks sections, RECHECK each picked section against ALL its relations — prerequisites, exclusions/not_for, related_sections, guardrails, court, and co-firing sections. Only after that recheck is the answer final. A section that fails its recheck is DROPPED with a reason, not kept. Then the legal terms are interconnected across sections.")
A("")
A("## Headline result — honest, and what it is (and is not)")
A("")
A("| | v1 | v2 |")
A("|---|---|---|")
A("| Adversarial suite (Lane 4, 34 layman questions) | 15/34 — **44.1%** | **33/34 — 97.1%** |")
A("| Kannada questions (5 of the 34) | 0/5 | **5/5** |")
A("| Sections (unique) | 29 | **32** (13 v1 statutory + 3 new: HMA 13, HMA 13B, Births & Deaths Act 1969 + 16 procedure) |")
A("| Nodes / edges | 38 / 66 | **46 / 77** (8 new nodes, 11 new edges) |")
A("| Layman phrases / Stage-1 mappings / synonyms | 0 / 0 / 0 | **126 / 19 / 156** |")
A("| Stage-2 recheck rules | 0 (notes only) | **121 checks across 16 sections** |")
A("")
A("**What the 97.1% is:** a graph-logic score from a mechanical walk in `merge_v2.py` — a disclosed token/substring matcher over Lane 1's phrasebook (NOT live Laya inference) + Lane 3's 121 recheck rules + the v2 fixes. Per-test facts were read off each question + Lane 4's notes and are listed below, so the re-run is reproducible. **It is NOT a live-model score:** no live Laya inference was run (torch/`laya` not installed, 440 MB RAM available), and no LLaMA 8B run exists. Do not quote 97.1% as a model accuracy.")
A("")
A("## The one remaining failure — and why it is a test-suite error, not a graph error")
A("")
A("**B4** (residence only, eviction threats, no money, no violence): v2 keeps `[PWDVA 17, PWDVA 18, PWDVA 19]`; Lane 4 expected `[PWDVA 17, PWDVA 19]`. **D8 has near-identical facts** (eviction threats, living there, no violence, no money asked) and Lane 4 expects PWDVA 18 there, with the note \"eviction threats are intimidation, which a protection order covers\". The two expected sets contradict each other on the same facts. v2 follows D8 (threats = intimidation → PWDVA 18 kept) and flags B4's expected set as the likely test-suite error. F3 (Kannada residence, same threats) also expects PWDVA 18, supporting D8.")
A("")
A("## Fixes applied in v2 (from Lane 4's 19 failures)")
A("")
A("1. **Kannada (A3, C4, F1, F2, F3):** Lane 1 phrasebook (21 Kannada phrases) + colloquial synonym map + `stage1:kannada-mapping` node. Was 0/5, now 5/5 on this suite — with the caveat that coverage is 21 formal phrases; phrasings outside the phrasebook still escalate.")
A("2. **HMA 13/13B unreturnable (A5, B6):** added as real sections with the divorce gate; HMA 13B conditional on mutual consent being stated.")
A("3. **Birth certificate (B5, D2):** added Registration of Births and Deaths Act 1969 as a real section; never HMA.")
A("4. **HMA 26 over-firing with no proceeding (B2, C1, D2):** `stage2:custody-no-proceeding-subset` — drop HMA 26, keep GWA 1890 + HMGA s.6 + welfare.")
A("5. **PWDVA leaf chain forcing PWDVA 20 (B4, D8):** `stage2:pwdva-per-section-gate` — each PWDVA section gated on its own trigger.")
A("6. **BNS 316 before any demand (D5):** `stage2:demand-gate` — demand first, then re-evaluate; BNS 316 escalated, HMA 27 stays live.")
A("7. **HMA 24 named with no proceeding (D6):** leaf gated; fallback to BNSS 144 as the live route.")
A("8. **Protection-only over-firing (D7):** PWDVA 20 now needs money actually asked for; violence alone is a protection claim (PWDVA 18). Criminal cruelty section for the beating itself stays in `unverified_excluded` — escalate, do not invent.")
A("9. **Vague question forcing 7 sections (D9):** `stage1:confidence-gate` — no facts → clarify/escalate, zero sections.")
A("10. **School fees under the wrong section (D10):** fees are a BNSS 144 child-maintenance head, not PWDVA 20.")
A("11. **Stranger-theft keyword trap (E2):** holder check — stranger holder drops Stridhan and falls through to all other checks (no early return).")
A("12. **C5 context:** `stage1:conversation-context` — facts from earlier turns persist; C5's question omits Stridhan but the case facts carry over.")
A("13. **Lane 1 defects found by Lane 6:** residence phrase listing HMA 26 as a candidate (school location does not create custody) — removed in v2; \"should I divorce\" mapping to HMA 13B with no consent fact — 13B now conditional on mutual consent.")
A("14. **Money negation (B4, D7, D8):** \"not asking for money\" / \"do not need money\" must not fire maintenance (Lane 2 negation handling, enforced in the matcher).")
A("")
A("## Per-question results (v2 walk)")
A("")
A("| ID | Lang | v2 kept | Expected | Verdict |")
A("|---|---|---|---|---|")
